      <p>How constraint-driven derivation works, from metaphor to mathematics.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="#the-constraint-thesis" class="series-card">
      <h3>The Constraint Thesis</h3>
      <p>Why constraints, not scale, determine intelligence.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="#safety-and-governance" class="series-card">
      <h3>Safety & Governance</h3>
      <p>How AI systems fail and how constraint governance prevents it.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="#the-hypostatic-boundary" class="series-card">
      <h3>The Hypostatic Boundary</h3>
      <p>The line between what a system does and what it is.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="#engineering" class="series-card">
      <h3>Engineering</h3>
      <p>Concrete artifacts that compile, pass tests, and run in production.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="#letters" class="series-card">
      <h3>Letters</h3>
      <p>Correspondence with researchers, applying the framework to their work.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>The Evidence</h2>
  <div class="evidence-grid">
    <div class="evidence-card">
      <h3>7 Resolvers</h3>
      <p>Claude, Grok 4, GPT 5.4, Gemini 3.1 Pro, DeepSeek v3.2 — all conform to the same seed</p>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-card">
      <h3>Haiku > Opus</h3>
      <p>The smallest model under constraints outperformed the largest model without them</p>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-card">
      <h3>53/54 Tests</h3>
      <p>A 1,057-line blind derivation from prose passes 53 of 54 tests designed for a separate implementation</p>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-card">
      <h3>p &lt; 10⁻¹⁰</h3>
      <p>Independent confirmation: theological framing eliminates shutdown resistance (ICMI 2026)</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>The Resolver</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">A governed conversational assistant running under the ENTRACE constraint stack. Bring your own API key. No data persisted. <a href="/doc/211-the-entrace-stack">Read the constraints it operates under.</a></p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a href="/resolve" class="btn btn-primary">Try the Resolver →</a>
    <a href="/doc/211-the-entrace-stack" class="btn btn-secondary">Read: ENTRACE Stack</a>
